.TH DWMBLOCKS 1 dwmblocks\-VERSION
.SH NAME
dwmblocks \- asynchronous status bar for dwm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dwmblocks
.RB [ \-\-help ]\ [ \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-\-all ]\ [ \-\-restart ]\ [ \-\-list ]\ [ \-\-update\ block ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
dwmblocks renders the dwm status bar out of independent blocks, each backed by a
shell script or binary. Blocks update on their own schedule and run asynchronously, so a
slow block never freezes the bar. Blocks are clickable: the
.B BLOCK_BUTTON
environment variable is set to the button number before the script runs (requires
dwm patched with
.UR https://dwm.suckless.org/patches/statuscmd/
statuscmd
.UE ).
.P
Run with no arguments, dwmblocks starts the status bar daemon. Run with any option
below, it instead acts as a client to the already running daemon.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Update all blocks.
.TP
.B \-\-restart
Restart the daemon.
.TP
.B \-\-list
Print configured block names, one per line.
.TP
.B \-\-update \fIblock\fR
Update the named block, e.g.
.RI "\(dq" "dwmblocks --update volume" \(dq .
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGRTMIN+n
Update the block whose config.h signal is
.IR n .
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Update all blocks.
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Terminate cleanly.
.SH USAGE
Run in the background at startup, e.g. from
.IR .xinitrc :
.RS
.EX
dwmblocks &
.EE
.RE
.SH CUSTOMIZATION
Blocks and display options are set in
.IR config.h ,
which must exist before building (copied from
.I config.def.h
on first
.BR make ).
Rebuild after any change; there is no runtime reload.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dwm (1)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/dimgerasimou/dwmasyncblocks
.UE .
